From 631f865a3823778684be7e90513e4f2996bc0a56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 17:09:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] v4l2_codec2: make hardware decode reach the screen under
 virtio

Adapts the component to a decoder presented by a device model rather
than by a real driver, and fixes the two reasons a correctly decoded
frame was never visible.

  * Ask the device for an RGBA capture format. The guest GL here is
    virgl on V3D and does not export GL_EXT_YUV_target, so an NV12
    EGLImage can never be sampled -- measured on hardware, the
    extension is simply absent from the compositor's list.

  * Pass the gralloc buffer's virgl resource id with each CAPTURE
    buffer, in v4l2_buffer.reserved2, so that the device model writes
    the decoded frame straight into the resource the compositor
    samples. The guest does not transfer the frame itself, and a
    gralloc lock would not do it either: that runs a transfer FROM the
    host first and discards what the decoder wrote.

The resource id comes from a virtgpu render node this component opens
itself. Every use of its GEM handles is made under one lock, because
the node and its handle cache are shared by all decoders in the
process.

Around those two:

  * QUERYBUF is skipped on the DMABUF queues, whose plane lengths come
    from the format instead, and a buffer is queued with at most one
    fd per V4L2 plane.
  * Capture formats are tried in this component's order of preference,
    and the frame pool is allocated with the negotiated format and the
    device's stride. The pixel format is declared
    (C2StreamPixelFormatInfo), and debug.v4l2codec2.output_delay can
    lower the H.264/HEVC output delay.
  * On a resolution change the CAPTURE queue is released before S_FMT.
  * Only the codecs a V4L2 device is present for are registered, and
    the service joins group camera, which owns /dev/video*.
  * Empty works are accepted and reported, output frames that arrive
    after a flush are dropped, and a block with a new id re-points a
    free V4L2 slot.
  * The frame pool keeps one graphic block fetched ahead, identifies a
    block without pool data by its dmabuf, and reports a failed fetch
    to the client instead of stalling: to the request waiting for it,
    or, for a fetch made ahead, to the next request.
  * The initial EOS buffer is RGBA when prefer_rgba is set, with a
    usage the gralloc accepts.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [depends on the downstream virtio-media device's
 reserved2 resource-id channel (qemu 0228) and on a guest GL without
 GL_EXT_YUV_target]
